            <ArticleTitle>Recent advances in nuclear cardiology. 2. Dynamic myocardial scintigraphy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>69-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nuclear cardiology, a developing subspeciality of cardiology and nuclear medicine, has experienced rapid growth during the past five years. Important advances in &quot;hot-spot&quot; and &quot;cold-spot&quot; myocardial scintigraphy for measurement of myocardial perfusion and detection of myocardial infarction are discussed in part 1 of this article, beginning on page 55. Part 2 concludes the discussion with an update on dynamic myocardial imaging.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
